# Recorded by record.sh from the text column. Every value is synthetic.
# Tab-separated: name, message type, the bytes protoc emitted in hex, the message in text format.
# One speech-to-text session in wire order: 8,000 Hz mu-law in frames of 20 to 40 ms, four
# utterances. The first ends in silence; a Finalize ends the second and the third, which is
# silent; the fourth is open when the client closes its sending half, which is not a frame.
# The last body before the first Finalize and before the half-close is shorter than a frame.
# One Accepted names no new input: it reports credit that returned. Each spoken utterance's
# last transcript segment ends at its endpoint.

